UPDATE companies SET description='Impact Plastics operates from Hamlet, North Carolina, as a custom sheet extrusion specialist focused on thermoforming packaging. The company serves the food packaging sector with an emphasis on barrier materials and precision thickness control.

The company runs advanced extrusion lines equipped with its visionX monitoring system, which provides real-time analysis of individual layer thickness during production. This precision gauge capability supports custom extruded sheet development for applications such as retort, form-fill-seal, and hot-fill processing. Impact Plastics also offers on-site technical support and dedicated engineering assistance for material qualification trials and commercialization projects.

Customers include food packaging manufacturers requiring barrier structures for shelf-stable and refrigerated products. The company’s materials are engineered for specific filling methods, sterilization processes, and shelf-life requirements, with experience across retort, FFS, and hot-fill applications.

Impact Plastics differentiates itself through its visionX real-time monitoring, a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015 and FSSC 22000, and a sustainability program built on reducing, reusing, and recycling waste. The team positions itself as an agile, entrepreneurial partner that collaborates from concept through commercialization.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','FSSC 22000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sheet extrusion", "Thermoforming packaging solutions", "Precision gauge monitoring (visionX system)", "Real-time layer thickness monitoring", "On-site technical support", "Material qualification trials", "Custom material development", "Sustainable manufacturing practices (reduce, reuse, recycle)", "Barrier food packaging development", "Retort packaging applications", "Form-fill-seal (FFS) packaging", "Hot-fill packaging applications"], "industries": ["Food packaging", "Barrier food packaging", "Thermoforming packaging", "Retort processing", "Form-fill-seal (FFS)", "Hot-fill processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["visionX system", "Precision gauge monitoring systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Real-time individual layer thickness monitoring via visionX system", "Dedicated technical support engineer assigned to every project", "ISO 9001:2015 and FSSC 22000 certified quality management system", "Sustainable operations focused on reducing, reusing, and recycling", "Custom sheet extrusion for barrier food packaging and thermoforming"], "facts_used": ["Location: Hamlet, North Carolina -> db", "Business: custom sheet extrusion for thermoforming packaging -> page \"/\"", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015 and FSSC 22000 -> page \"/quality\"", "Technology: visionX system for real-time layer thickness monitoring -> page \"/quality\"", "Services: on-site technical support and dedicated technical support engineer -> page \"/quality\"", "Applications: retort, FFS, hot-fill processing -> page \"/quality\"", "Sustainability: reducing, reusing, recycling practices -> page \"/\"", "Industries: food packaging, barrier food packaging -> page \"/about-us\" and \"/quality\""], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom sheet extrusion industry", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='impact-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Imperial Electronic Assembly was founded in 1989 in Brookfield, Connecticut, and has remained a family-owned operation since its inception. The company began as a privately held contract electronic manufacturing service provider, built on the principle that long-term relationships drive success.

Today the firm delivers end-to-end electronic manufacturing services, including collaborative engineering, prototyping, printed circuit board assembly, functional testing, and full supply-chain logistics. Its capabilities span design collaboration, project management, and quality assurance, allowing it to take projects from concept through volume production without outsourcing core processes.

Imperial serves a diverse customer base across medical, military, security, energy, and telecommunications sectors. The company notes it has designed and built products for dozens of industries since 1989, with specific experience in regulated environments such as medical devices and defense equipment.

