UPDATE companies SET description='Incap Electronics US, Inc. operates from a 6,500-square-meter facility in Coal Center, Pennsylvania. The site has over 26 years of electronics manufacturing experience and employs 124 people. It is the U.S. arm of Incap Corporation, a global EMS provider listed on Nasdaq Helsinki since 1997, and is led by Managing Director David Spehar.

The facility specializes in complex printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) using advanced surface-mount and through-hole technologies, supported by in-circuit testing, functional testing, validation, conformal coating, selective soldering, and precision assembly. Engineering services include design for manufacturability, test development, prototyping, new product introduction, hardware and software development, embedded systems, industrial IoT, and power electronics R&D. The company also provides mechatronics, cable and wire harness assembly, magnetic assembly, electronics protection, box build, control cabinets, clean room production, and automotive-grade EMS. Full product support covers global sourcing, fast-track programs, customized solutions, final configuration, fulfillment, and after-sales MRO.

Incap US serves customers in energy, power and charging; defence and aerospace; and e-mobility and automotive sectors. Typical applications include metering infrastructure, gas detection systems, industrial electronics and control systems, medical devices, and sensor-based technologies. The company emphasizes long-term partnerships, with many customer relationships exceeding 20 years.

Incap US differentiates itself through a local, customer-driven approach backed by a global manufacturing network. The team prioritizes fast decision-making, direct communication, and proactive problem-solving to keep production running smoothly. A focus on process control, robust testing, and product stability aims to deliver total cost of ownership and long-term reliability over short-term cost optimization.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015','ISO 45001:2018','ISO 13485:2016','ANSI/ESD S20.20:2021','10CFR 50 Appendix B','10CFR Part 21','IATF 16949','AS 9100D','NADCAP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (SMT)", "PCB assembly (THT)", "Complex PCBA (high-density, high-reliability)", "In-circuit testing (ICT)", "Functional testing (FCT)", "Validation testing", "Conformal coating", "Selective soldering", "Precision assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Test development", "Repair and rework", "Lifecycle support", "Prototyping", "New product introduction (NPI)", "Hardware development", "Software development", "Embedded systems development", "Industrial IoT development", "Power electronics R&D", "Mechatronics & electromechanics assembly", "Cable & wire harness assembly", "Box build", "Control cabinets"], "industries": ["Energy, power & charging", "Defence & aerospace", "E-mobility & automotive", "Medical devices", "Industrial electronics", "Sensor technologies"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Medium-volume production with high SMT content", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Long-term partnerships with customers spanning 20+ years", "Fast decision-making and proactive, direct communication", "Local U.S. facility with access to global manufacturing network", "Advanced testing capabilities including ICT, functional test, and validation", "Medium-volume production expertise with high SMT content"], "facts_used": ["Location: Coal Center, Pennsylvania -> /", "Facility size: 6,500 m\u00b2 -> /", "Empl