UPDATE companies SET description='Indusco Wire Rope & Fittings, based in Baltimore, Maryland, has operated under the Mazzella Companies since its acquisition in 2011. Mazzella was founded in 1954 by James Mazzella in Cleveland, Ohio, and remains a privately held, family-owned business. The merger formalizes a long-standing relationship, with Indusco becoming part of Mazzella''s Industrial Distribution/Reseller Division effective August 2025.

The company supplies a broad range of lifting and rigging products, including wire rope, slings and assemblies, rigging hardware, cordage, fall protection, and engineered lifting devices. It also fabricates overhead cranes, provides crane and hoist service and repair, and offers OSHA-mandated inspections and rigging training.

