UPDATE companies SET description='Intelligent Manufacturing Solutions (IMS) was founded in 2005 in Londonderry, New Hampshire. The company was purpose-built to address a service gap for high-quality, rapid prototype and small-lot printed circuit board assembly. In December 2024, IMS was acquired by Perimeter Solutions (NYSE: PRM), which aims to broaden its portfolio and add a new business model for acquiring and supporting OEM legacy product lines.

IMS provides full life-cycle electronics assembly services, including rapid prototype assembly, high-mix flexible manufacturing, design-for-manufacturing (DFM) analysis, end-of-life support, box build, short-notice production, and build-to-order manufacturing. The New England facility houses multiple SMT pick-and-place lines (Mycronic MY300, M100, MY9E), three Heller 1808 MkIII reflow ovens, solder paste inspection and deposition equipment (Mycronic Primo 3D SPI, MY600, MY500, SpeedPrint SP710, MPM Accuflex), X-ray and AOI inspection (UniComp AX8200, Mirtec MV6 Omni), rework stations (VJ Electronics Summit), selective soldering (Nordson Novo 103, Ace 102, Hollis TDL wave), and aqueous cleaning systems. The company emphasizes quick turnaround, stating it can start production the day an order is received and ship assemblies within hours. No specific headcount or facility square footage is disclosed.

IMS serves aerospace and defense, medical and instrumentation, communications, consumer electronics/IoT, automotive, and industrial sectors. Customer testimonials cite an automotive technology company, a consumer robotics company, and an IoT solutions provider. The company supports OEMs needing rapid prototyping, low-volume production, and end-of-life product sustainment.

IMS was started to fill a market gap for responsive, high-quality prototype and low-volume PCBA services. The company differentiates itself through a culture of responsiveness, on-time delivery, and a direct order fulfillment model that helps customers grow. Its acquisition by Perimeter Solutions adds a model for acquiring and licensing OEM legacy product lines to sustain them through their remaining lifecycle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rapid prototype assembly", "Box build", "High-mix flexible manufacturing", "Design for manufacturing (DFM) analysis", "End-of-life support", "Quality assurance", "IP acquisition and legacy product sustainment", "Short-notice production", "Build-to-order manufacturing", "Component sourcing", "SMT assembly", "Through-hole soldering", "Selective soldering", "Wave soldering", "X-ray inspection", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "Rework and repair", "Aqueous cleaning", "Programming, labeling, and packaging"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical & Instrumentation", "Communications", "Consumer Electronics/IoT", "Automotive", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Mycronic MY300 SX14 (30,000 cph)", "Mycronic M100 SX14 (25,000 cph each) \u2013 2 units", "Mycronic MY9E (15,000 cph)", "Heller 1808 MkIII reflow ovens \u2013 3 units", "Mycronic Primo 3D solder paste inspection", "Mycronic MY600 deposition with vision and repair", "Mycronic MY500 deposition with vision and repair", "SpeedPrint SP710 advanced vision intelligence \u2013 2 units", "MPM Accuflex dual system", "UniComp AX8200 programmable X-ray 2D/3D modeling 130kV", "Mirtec MV6 Omni 3D AOI \u2013 2 units", "VJ Electronics Summit 1100HR rework", "VJ Electronics Summit 1800HRE rework", "Nordson Novo 103 selective soldering (Pb-free)", "Ace 102 selective soldering (Pb)", "Hollis TDL wave solder (Pb-free)", "Aqueous Technologies Trident Trio triple batch cleaner (Kyzen A4639)", "AquaKleen auto stencil cleaner SC1550", "Nordson-Da