UPDATE companies SET description='Iron Work Studio operates from Owings, Maryland, where it has been based for over two decades. The company was founded in 1997 by Rob Link, a third‑generation welder who started with a 200‑square‑foot warehouse in nearby Severn before moving the shop closer to home. Link, who holds a technical degree in electronic engineering and a background in the steamfitters’ union, built the business from the ground up, purchasing equipment and hiring a full‑time crew as demand grew.

The studio produces custom ironwork for residential clients, ranging from fine‑art pieces such as chandeliers, tables, and railings to large‑scale architectural installations. Core processes include welding, fabricating, CNC plasma cutting, and computer‑aided design using AutoCAD. A four‑person team handles projects from initial drawings through final assembly, working with iron, steel, and sheet metal in a shop equipped with a CNC plasma cutting machine.

