UPDATE companies SET description='Ironwood Mills operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where founder Scott Mills established the company in 2016. After more than two decades as an independent contractor, Mills turned a lifelong fascination with wood—sparked by a tool kit at age six—into a business that rescues discarded trees from the Phoenix metro area and transforms them into custom furniture and live‑edge slabs. The “urban lumber” model began with Mills personally hunting for unique logs in the desert, a practice that now feeds a small team of woodworkers.

The shop at 8342 N. 7th Street houses a Lucas Mill 10‑30 (cuts logs up to 5′ diameter, 21′ long), a hydraulic Wood‑Mizer bandsaw, a Wood Wizz surfacing machine (up to 7 × 17 feet), and an iDRY vacuum kiln. Services include custom furniture fabrication, milling ($150/hour, one‑hour minimum), machine surfacing ($150/hour), and kiln drying ($2/board foot, 1,000‑board‑foot minimum). The team—Mills, Kit Vander Jagt (20 years’ experience), and Michael Toret (10+ years, including theatrical scenery and welding)—produces one‑off pieces and small batches.

Primary customers are interior designers, architects, professional woodworkers, and homeowners. Designers source slabs and collaborate on custom tables and specialty items; woodworkers bring material for surfacing and kiln drying; homeowners commission finished furniture. The company also hosts team‑building workshops.

Ironwood Mills differentiates itself through its urban‑lumber supply chain—turning neighborhood trees that would otherwise be chipped into furniture‑grade material—and through vacuum‑kiln drying that eliminates raised grain and reduces drying time. Mills describes the mission as a privilege: “to take a forgotten & unwanted tree and bring it back to life.”', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture fabrication", "Log milling (Lucas Mill 10\u201130)", "Bandsaw milling (Wood\u2011Mizer)", "Machine surfacing (Wood Wizz)", "Vacuum kiln drying (iDRY)", "Live\u2011edge slab production", "Table base fabrication", "Urban lumber processing", "Woodworking workshops"], "industries": ["Furniture manufacturing", "Interior design", "Architecture", "Woodworking", "Residential construction", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Arizona hardwoods (Acacia, Ash, Carob, Chinaberry, Cork Bark Oak, Elm, Eucalyptus, Ficus, Hickory, Indian Rosewood, Juniper, Mesquite, Olive, Pine, Silk Oak, Sycamore)", "Urban lumber", "Recycled lumber", "Live-edge slabs"], "equipment": ["Lucas Mill 10\u201130", "Wood\u2011Mizer bandsaw mill", "Wood Wizz surfacing machine", "iDRY vacuum kiln"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Urban lumber supply chain: rescues discarded Phoenix-area trees", "Lucas Mill 10\u201130 cuts logs up to 5\u2032 diameter and 21\u2032 long", "Wood Wizz surfacing machine handles slabs up to 7\u202f\u00d7\u202f17\u202ffeet", "iDRY vacuum kiln dries lumber to precise moisture content", "Custom furniture built by a team with 20+ years\u2019 combined experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2016 -> db", "Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Founder Scott Mills -> /about", "Scott Mills background: 20+ years independent contractor, tool kit at age 6 -> /about", "Urban lumber model: rescues discarded trees from Phoenix area -> /, /about", "Team members: Kit Vander Jagt (20 years woodworking), Michael Toret (10+ years, thea